<title>USA: U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CDT, boxed beef was uneven on light to moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib and loin cuts generally were steady while chuck and round cuts steady to firm. Beef trimmings were generally steady on light demand. -- USDA</p>
<p>  149 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>    3 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>15 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     103.56	103.18	 96.64	 95.82</p>
<p>Change	    0.11	 -0.08	  0.48	  0.40</p>
<p>Rib	  165.19	164.46	146.56	144.65</p>
<p>Chuck	 71.60	 71.20	 72.01	 70.30</p>
<p>Round	 90.87	 90.87	 87.92	 87.92</p>
<p>Loin	 161.26	160.43	140.69	140.23</p>
<p>Brisket     59.00	 59.00	 59.89	 59.89</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  64.40	 64.32	 64.63	 64.46</p>
